            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:1",
            "text": "Khoomei, a traditional art form from Mongolia, is known as a kind of throat singing. It’s an ancient vocal tradition which allows singers to produce the sounds of multiple notes simultaneously（同时地）in their throats. And it creates a sound that/ which echoes the natural world – from the howling wind to the rumbling river."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "Khoomei has been passed down through generations of Mongolians and is closely tied to their spiritual and cultural practices. Its ability to mimic（模仿）the sounds of nature reflects a deep connection to the land, demonstrating the vastness and beauty of the grasslands."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "In 2009, khoomei was recognized by UNESCO as an Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, highlighting its significance as a vital part of the world’s cultural heritage. This acknowledgement not only honors its cultural importance but also raises awareness of the ongoing need to preserve the ancient art form. Ever since, the recognition has fuel(l) ed efforts to ensure it continues to develop in modern society."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "One of khoomei’s remarkable qualities is its ability to transcend（超越）generations. While/ Though/ Although it has traditionally been performed by senior masters, the art form has increasingly captured the interest of younger generations."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:5",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-wuxi-2026-01-senior-three-first-semester-final-quality-survey:grammar-fill:5",
            "text": "The appearance of khoomei in popular reality shows and movies has helped raise its profile among a wider audience. The hit animated movie Ne Zha 2, for example, features the distinctive sound, especially during mythical moments, such as the appearance of the Tianyuan Ding. Sung by Halamuji, a young Mongolian artist, it contributes significantly to the atmosphere."
          }
